## Prototype Stack (Buildable Now)

| Component | Implementation |
|---|---|
| Capture | Whisper / Deepgram (speech-to-text) |
| Embedding | e5-large, BGE, or equivalent sentence transformer |
| Vector storage | FAISS, sqlite-vec, or Weaviate |
| 3D projection | UMAP (high-dim → 3D lattice coordinates) |
| Encryption | CRYSTALS-Kyber (ML-KEM) wrapped by butterfly-derived KDF |
| Spatial DB | Neo4j or custom graph store with 3D coordinate indexing |
| VR runtime | Unity on Quest 3 / Vision Pro |
| Conversational layer | RAG pipeline with streaming LLM inference |

---

## Endgame Extensions

**Physical quartz archival:** Replace digital storage backend with actual 5D optical quartz writing for permanent archival. Current constraint is write speed and equipment cost, not feasibility.

**Moiré materials as physical key medium:** Twisted bilayer graphene and similar moiré superlattice materials exhibit measurable Hofstadter butterfly spectra under applied magnetic fields (Dean et al., Nature 2013). A far-future version could read memory-access states from a real quantum lattice rather than simulating one computationally — the key derivation function instantiated in actual condensed-matter physics.

**Key references:**
- Dean et al., "Hofstadter's butterfly and the fractal quantum Hall effect in moiré superlattices" (Nature, 2013)

---

## Summary

The Memory Lattice combines five established technologies — vector embeddings, 5D optical storage, fractal-derived key hierarchies, spatial graph databases, and VR rendering — into a unified architecture where encryption, addressing, and navigation are aspects of a single mathematical structure. Every component exists independently in production or demonstrated research. The design contribution is the integration: a system where a passphrase becomes a coordinate, a coordinate becomes a key, a key becomes a path, and a path becomes a way of walking through everything you remember.
